i## Introduction	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iI was writing some notes in GNU Emacs and thought it might	/	tilde.club	70
ibe fun to create a small, personal, pocket-sized tool for	/	tilde.club	70
imanaging notes in a simple way. GNU Emacs is very	/	tilde.club	70
icomprehensive and well-suited for managing notes, I've been	/	tilde.club	70
iusing it for several years to write my zettelkasten.	/	tilde.club	70
iHowever, I wanted to try a different note-taking tool. After	/	tilde.club	70
idoing some research, I realized it made more sense to write	/	tilde.club	70
imy own tool that would meet my specific criteria.	/	tilde.club	70
hGNU Emacs	URL:https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs	www.gnu.org	443
i	/	tilde.club	70
iIn this blog post, I explain my research journey leading up	/	tilde.club	70
ito the creation of my own personal note-taking tool. If you'd	/	tilde.club	70
ilike more technical details, feel free to check out the	/	tilde.club	70
iproject's technical documentation available in the GitHub	/	tilde.club	70
irepository.	/	tilde.club	70
hGitHub repository	URL:https://github.com/theobori/a	github.com	443
