i## My needs	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iThis section describes my needs.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i### File format independence	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iI want the file format of the notes to be independent of the	/	tilde.club	70
itool. I want to write in Markdown, Org, or even plain text.	/	tilde.club	70
iThe tool does not support relationships between notes, this	/	tilde.club	70
ifunctionality will rely entirely on the file format.	/	tilde.club	70
hMarkdown	URL:https://commonmark.org/	commonmark.org	443
hOrg	URL:https://orgmode.org/fr/	orgmode.org	443
i	/	tilde.club	70
i### File naming scheme	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iI want each note to have metadata embedded in its file name.	/	tilde.club	70
iAt a minimum, I want each note to have a title, tags, and a	/	tilde.club	70
ifile extension.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i### Flexible file hierarchy	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iNote files should be able to reside in a flat directory	/	tilde.club	70
istructure or in subfolders with an undefined maximum depth.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i### Dedicated query language	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iThe idea is to have a dedicated query language for filtering	/	tilde.club	70
inotes. Ideally, the query should be compiled into bytecode	/	tilde.club	70
ifor a virtual machine, and then the bytecode should be	/	tilde.club	70
iexecuted for each note by passing the context. I want to be	/	tilde.club	70
iable to filter by at least title, tags, and modification	/	tilde.club	70
idate.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i### Simplicity	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iI want the tool to be easy to use and intuitive. I'd like it	/	tilde.club	70
iso that even if I stop using the tool for three years, I can	/	tilde.club	70
ifigure out how it works very quickly. It should support only	/	tilde.club	70
ibasic features, that is, creating, renaming, editing, and	/	tilde.club	70
ifiltering notes.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i## Search for existing software	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iI looked into well-known note-taking software, Obsidian,	/	tilde.club	70
iNotion, Joplin, but didn't find anything that quite fit the	/	tilde.club	70
ibill. They were complex, overloaded, commercially oriented,	/	tilde.club	70
iAI oriented, had unnecessary features, or weren't cross-	/	tilde.club	70
iplatform. The closest thing to what I'm looking for is zk.	/	tilde.club	70
