i## Inspiration	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iI usually use GNU Emacs, so I decided to explore packages	/	tilde.club	70
ispecialized in note-taking and metadata filtering.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i### denote.el	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iDenote.el is the Emacs package that comes closest to what I	/	tilde.club	70
iwas looking for. It's a simple tool that uses filenames to	/	tilde.club	70
iinfer certain metadata. I drew inspiration from the filename	/	tilde.club	70
ischema.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i### org-ql	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iI stumbled upon org-ql by chance, it lets you search for	/	tilde.club	70
inotes using a custom query language that inspired me. It's a	/	tilde.club	70
ifunctional-style language similar to Emacs Lisp, it's used to	/	tilde.club	70
ifilter notes by their metadata and implements basic binary	/	tilde.club	70
ioperations.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i## My personal tool	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
iSo I wrote a CLI that lets me create, rename, edit, and	/	tilde.club	70
ifilter my notes using my custom language. Below is an	/	tilde.club	70
iexample of a language expression.	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i(or	/	tilde.club	70
i  (or 	/	tilde.club	70
i    (title "title1")	/	tilde.club	70
i    (title "title2"))	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i  (tag "tag1")	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i  (if (from-date "2020-01-01")	/	tilde.club	70
i    (title "title3")	/	tilde.club	70
i  (title "title4"))	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i  (to-date "2020-02-01")	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
i  (and	/	tilde.club	70
i    (not (tag "tag2"))	/	tilde.club	70
i    (tag "tag3")))	/	tilde.club	70
i	/	tilde.club	70
